 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? That's fine. You can cook them in the pan, the same way you would a steak. Then keep the oven on. Put pan on a middle shelf and turn the stove on with it. Keep the heat low, like barely simmering. The oven keeps the heat steady. Just put a small plate in the pan, and if steam is coming up past the sticks, the oven's hot enough. That's a fair point. Sticks on the plate are the only thing that matters. Some people use combs to cut them.",
